WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.232
Albert Einstein left Germany in 1933 as

2
00:00:03.232 --> 00:00:06.616
the Nazis came to power, and never went back.

3
00:00:06.966 --> 00:00:12.056
He settled at the Institute for Advanced Study in Princeton, filed his

4
00:00:12.056 --> 00:00:17.073
first citizenship papers in 1936, and took the oath as an American in

5
00:00:17.073 --> 00:00:22.454
1940 — one of the few immigrants whose surname became a byword for genius.

6
00:00:22.803 --> 00:00:26.307
In 1905, working as a clerk in the Swiss patent office

7
00:00:26.307 --> 00:00:29.746
in Bern, he published the papers that remade physics.

8
00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:33.704
Einstein held professorships in Zurich, Prague and

9
00:00:33.704 --> 00:00:38.177
Berlin, and in 1921 he was awarded the Nobel Prize in Physics.

10
00:00:38.527 --> 00:00:41.956
He used his fame as an American deliberately: for refugees

11
00:00:41.956 --> 00:00:45.325
fleeing the same Europe he had escaped, for civil rights,

12
00:00:45.325 --> 00:00:48.813
and against the misuse of the physics he had helped create.

13
00:00:49.163 --> 00:00:51.880
Read the full story, with every source, on this page.
